.TH RDP-LAUNCHER 1 "2026-11-23" "rdp-launcher 0.0.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rdp-launcher \- open a remote desktop to a saved machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rdp-launcher
.I host
.br
.B rdp-launcher
.BR pick " | " new " | " list " | " doctor
.br
.B rdp-launcher
.BR test " | " add " | " remove " | " set-password " | " forget-password " | " connect
.I host
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each machine is a small text file,
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rdp-launcher/hosts/host.conf
(default
.IR ~/.config/rdp-launcher/hosts/ ).
.B rdp-launcher
tries the host's addresses in order, uses the first one that answers, takes the
password from the system password store, and starts FreeRDP (or, on macOS,
Microsoft Windows App). Options, including the password, reach FreeRDP through a
pipe, never on the command line.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I host
Connect.
.TP
.B pick
Show a dialog: \(lqNew connection\&...\(rq, the saved hosts (most recently used
first), and \(lqRemove a saved connection\&...\(rq. Missing usernames and
passwords are asked for in dialogs; a password is kept only when you choose
\(lqSave & Connect\(rq. Errors appear as dialogs.
.TP
.B new
Ask for an address (\fIhost\fR, \fIhost\fR:\fIport\fR or [\fIv6\fR]:\fIport\fR),
save it as a host, and connect.
.TP
.BI open " file.rdp"
Connect using an .rdp file (also accepted as the only argument). The host is
added to the saved list with an
.B rdpfile
entry, and FreeRDP loads the file's other settings.
.TP
.BI remove " host"
Delete a saved host and its stored password.
.TP
.B list
List hosts and whether each answers now.
.TP
.BI test " host"
Probe every address of a host and report each one. Does not log in.
.TP
.BI add " host"
Create a host file from the built-in template and open it in
.BR $VISUAL / $EDITOR .
.TP
.BI set-password " host"
Store the RDP password (macOS Keychain via
.BR security ;
elsewhere the Secret Service via
.BR secret-tool ).
The tool itself prompts for the password, with echo off.
.TP
.BI forget-password " host"
Remove the stored password.
.TP
.B doctor
Report what this machine has: config dir, FreeRDP binary, password tool, dialog tool.
.SH HOST FILE
.nf
name      = My PC
addresses = mypc.local 192.168.1.30
port      = 3389
user      = me
client    = freerdp            # or windows-app (macOS)
args      = /dynamic-resolution
env       = SDL_RENDER_VSYNC=1  # NAME=value, added to FreeRDP's environment
.fi
.PP
A
.B #
at the start of a line or after a blank starts a comment. Values in
.B addresses
and
.BR args " and " env
are split on blanks (no quoting).
.PP
On macOS, FreeRDP is started with
.B SDL_RENDER_VSYNC=1
(frames shown in step with the display) unless the environment or the host's
.B env
line sets it; see the README's macOS notes. Use
.B env = SDL_RENDER_VSYNC=0
to turn it off.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RDP_LAUNCHER_FREERDP
FreeRDP binary to use instead of searching for sdl-freerdp3, sdl-freerdp, xfreerdp3, xfreerdp.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directories for host files and for the per-host FreeRDP log written by
.BR pick .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok, 1 failure, 2 usage, 3 host file problem, 4 host unreachable,
5 no RDP client, 6 password store problem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xfreerdp (1),
.BR secret-tool (1),
.BR security (1)
